<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Archivingdigital Policy - AJSMR</title><style>body{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;margin:0;background:#f5f6f8;color:#222;line-height:1.65}.container{max-width:1050px;margin:35px auto;padding:0 20px}.card{background:#fff;border-radius:8px;padding:32px;box-shadow:0 2px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.08)}h1{margin-top:0;color:#222;font-size:30px}h2{font-size:21px;margin-top:28px;color:#333}li{margin:8px 0}.note{background:#f0f4f8;padding:14px 16px;border-left:4px solid #555;margin:20px 0}.small{font-size:13px;color:#666}</style></head><body><div class="container"><div class="card"><h1>Archiving & Digital Preservation Policy</h1><div class="note">AJSMR is committed to maintaining long-term access to its published scholarly record.</div><h2>Purpose</h2><p>This policy describes how AJSMR seeks to preserve published articles and issues so that the scholarly record remains accessible over the long term.</p><h2>Online Availability</h2><p>Published articles and issues are intended to remain freely accessible through the AJSMR website. Article-level pages should provide stable landing pages and access to published full text.</p><h2>Digital Preservation</h2><p>AJSMR should maintain copies of published content in a recognized long-term digital preservation or archiving service.</p><p><strong>Testing note:</strong> No specific preservation service is named until the publisher confirms the actual service in use.</p><h2>Continuity</h2><p>If the journal website or publishing platform changes, reasonable measures should preserve published articles, metadata, identifiers and issue records.</p><h2>Self-Archiving</h2><p>Authors may deposit permitted versions of their work in repositories in accordance with the journal's Open Access, Copyright & Self-Archiving Policy.</p><h2>Persistent Identifiers</h2><p>Where a DOI or other persistent identifier is assigned, the article landing page should remain associated with that identifier and resolve to the authoritative article location.</p><p class="small">AJSMR local testing version. Final wording should be confirmed against actual journal practices before live publication.</p></div></div></body></html>